            <ArticleTitle>Acute myocardial infarction and thyrotoxic storm--a difficult and dangerous combination.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>707-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe an unusual case of acute myocardial infarction (AMI) and cardiogenic shock in a 25-year-old woman. After coronary revascularization, a thyrotoxic storm developed and the patient's cardiac failure changed into a hyperdynamic circulation without obvious changes in the patient's vital signs. This report will focus on three issues: (1) the benefit of advanced hemodynamic monitoring in circulatory unstable patients, (2) the confounding effects of untreated hyperthyroidism on the circulation, and (3) previous cancer treatment as a cause of AMI in young persons.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
